        "original_id": "5354292e-1acb-5c78-b956-1d6ec5cb488d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Cases: Everson v. Board of Education; Rasul v. Bush\n- Organizations: United States Supreme Court\n- Concepts: Establishment Clause; Bill of Rights; state law; habeas corpus; Guantanamo Bay detention camp; detention legality\n\nFacts:\n- In 1947, Everson v. Board of Education, 330 U.S. 1, was a landmark United States Supreme Court decision.\n- Everson v. Board of Education held that the Establishment Clause in the United States Bill of Rights applied to state law.\n- In 2004, Rasul v. Bush, 542 U.S. 466, was a landmark United States Supreme Court decision.\n- Rasul v. Bush held that foreign nationals detained at the Guantanamo Bay detention camp could petition federal courts for writs of habeas corpus to challenge the legality of their detention.",
